---
import MaterialsTable from '@/components/ui/MaterialsTable.astro';
import SpiralSpring from '@/components/diagrams/SpiralSpring.astro';
import Todo from '@/components/ui/Todo.astro';
import { spiral } from '@/data/products';
import ProductLayout from '@/layouts/ProductLayout.astro';

export const prerender = false;

if (import.meta.env.DEV !== true && import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SHOW_TODOS !== 'true') {
  return new Response(null, { status: 404 });
}
---

<ProductLayout product={spiral}>
  <Fragment slot="about">
    <p>
      This page is a <strong>draft</strong>. The client lists spiral springs among the parts they
      make, together with conical springs. What “spiral” means here is not yet confirmed: a wire
      wound in a flat spiral, or a flat-strip power / clock spring.
    </p>
    <Todo
      block
      text="confirm whether spiral means wire spiral or flat-strip power spring, then rewrite this page."
    />
    <p>
      Until then: send the drawing or the old part. If it is in our 0.40–2.50 mm wire range we can
      usually help. A wide flat strip may be outside what the machines here do.
    </p>
    <p>
      The drawing on this page is a generic wire spiral with an arbor tab and an outer hook. It is
      there as a generic drawing until the part family is confirmed.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="types">
    <figure class="type-fig max-w-[28rem]">
      <div class="bp-grid type-draw">
        <SpiralSpring annotated />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Generic spiral — replace once the part family is confirmed.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Fragment>

  <MaterialsTable slot="materials" />

  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <p>
      A photo of the part, a ruler in the frame, and the quantity are enough for a first reply. Mark
      the arbor and the outer hook if they have to fit existing pins.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="applications">
    <p>
      We will list typical uses once we know which spiral we make. Do not assume clock springs,
      brush springs or constant-force strip from this page.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .type-fig {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .type-draw {
    padding: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-grid);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    color: var(--color-navy-900);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
